# Plain Punctuation (Quotes and Dashes)

When writing plans, docs, changelogs, comments, or any other markdown (and in code comments), use plain ASCII punctuation only.

## Quotes

Do not use smart / curly quotes. Use straight quotes only.

| Avoid | Use |
|-------|-----|
| `“` `”` (U+201C / U+201D) | `"` |
| `‘` `’` (U+2018 / U+2019) | `'` |

```markdown
<!-- BAD -->
schema mixes “who changed” with “done counts”

<!-- GOOD -->
schema mixes "who changed" with "done counts"
```

Apostrophes in contractions/possessives: use straight `'` (e.g. `Dashboard's`, `don't`), not `’`.

## Dashes

Do not use emdash (`—`, U+2014) or endash (`–`, U+2013).

- Prefer a spaced double hyphen for a dash or mid-sentence break: ` -- `.
- A single hyphen (`-`) is fine for list markers, compound words, and simple separators where you would normally write a hyphen.

```markdown
<!-- BAD -->
Status: design only — not implemented
Updated sorting – now respects priority markers.

<!-- GOOD -->
Status: design only -- not implemented
Updated sorting -- now respects priority markers.

<!-- GOOD (list / hyphen) -->
- First item
noteChangedAtMs
```

For a mid-sentence subclause, use a pair of spaced double hyphens:

```markdown
The filter -- when enabled -- hides completed items.
```
